WEBVTT

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.840
Your Turnly sales portal keeps each

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.800
sales conversation organized.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.730
Overview brings your prospect list,

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.330
calling, purchase links, and

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.610
follow-ups together.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.250
These are actual portal screens with

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.950
fictional training records.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.370
Check your open prospects,

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.880
follow-ups due, and completed

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:15.840
purchases.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.210
Completed purchases come from

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.080
confirmed gift-card payments.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.900
Changing a lead's stage by hand does

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.440
not create a paid order.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.080
Some navigation has changed since

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.200
these screenshots: Team is now admin

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:26.930
only.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:28.660
Complete Onboarding and the playbook

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.120
before you begin outreach.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.980
Find your personal checkout link.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.510
Scroll to Your link.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.070
Your credited sales.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:36.370
Copy link puts your personal

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.890
gift-card checkout address on your

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:38.790
clipboard.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.220
Use your own link so a completed

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.180
purchase can be attributed to you.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.190
Email a contact and Text a contact

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.690
open the sending form.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.210
This example link is for training

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:47.960
only.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.770
In your account, use the real link

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.740
shown here.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.050
Choose a prospect.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.150
Open Prospects in the left menu.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:55.800
Use the search box and filters to

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.230
find the person you need.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.730
My leads limits the view to your

00:00:58.730 --> 00:00:59.740
assignments.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.120
Filter by stage when you want to

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.770
work new prospects first.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.730
Review the name and contact details,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.640
then choose Work prospect.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.440
Start calling opens the lead-working

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.050
flow; it does not automatically

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.500
place a telephone call.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.000
Prepare the conversation.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.680
The lead workspace puts contact

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.190
details on the left and your

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.120
conversation outcome on the right.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.360
Read the saved notes before

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.800
contacting someone.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.860
Use Edit primary details to correct

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.040
a name, email, or phone number.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.640
Open scripts and objections gives

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.340
you conversation guidance.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.300
Ask about upcoming closings, current

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.770
closing gifts, and whether their

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.490
clients live within Turnly's service

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:34.180
area.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.940
Call without leaving the portal.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.420
Click Call lead beside the phone

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.160
number.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.630
The call panel opens at the lower

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.390
right.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.560
Check that it names the correct

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.610
prospect, then click Start call when

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:44.490
you are ready.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:45.930
Allow microphone access in your

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.680
browser and use a headset.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.520
Once connected, the panel provides

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.120
mute, keypad, and hang-up controls.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.170
End the call before navigating away.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.900
Recent calls to this lead shows call

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:56.800
results.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.390
If dialing is blocked by a budget

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:00.540
limit, contact your administrator.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.140
Email the gift-card link.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.560
Choose Email link in the lead

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.600
workspace.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.460
Confirm the selected contact and the

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:07.880
destination email.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:09.280
The message includes your tracked

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.890
checkout link and the contact's

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:11.580
name.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.300
Check the consent box only after

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.960
verifying that the recipient agreed

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.610
to receive Turnly emails at that

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.530
address.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.290
Then choose Send email.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.800
A provider acceptance means the

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.220
sending service accepted the

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:23.930
message; it does not guarantee

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:24.810
delivery.

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.300
No message is being sent in this

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.130
training.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.850
Text the right recipient.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.520
Text link uses the phone number

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.880
saved on the lead.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.220
If the person asks you to use

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.080
another number, choose Send to

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.180
different number.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.080
Enter that number, confirm consent

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.930
for texts to that number, then

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.860
scroll down to Send text.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.600
This override applies only to that

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.380
message; it does not change the

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.650
saved contact.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.100
Send to different email works the

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.630
same way for email.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.360
Never use an alternate recipient to

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.890
bypass an opt-out.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.310
Save notes and honor opt-outs.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.060
After the conversation, select the

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.200
accurate Outcome or Stage, add a

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.040
useful conversation note, and click

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.510
Save conversation.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.630
Follow-up and Not interested move

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:06.250
the lead out of the active pipeline

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.950
and into the follow-up flow.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.580
The first reminder is due in thirty

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.360
days.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.960
If the person says not to contact

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.860
them again, select the red Do Not

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.920
Contact checkbox and save.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.760
That permanently stops outreach and

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.690
removes the lead from follow-ups.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.250
Work the follow-up banks.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.020
Open Follow-ups to see the age-based

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:23.830
groups.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.780
Thirty-day means zero through thirty

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:26.610
days.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.400
Sixty-day means thirty-one through

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.250
sixty.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.150
Ninety-day means sixty-one through

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:31.970
ninety.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.740
Long term means ninety-one days or

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:34.450
more.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.860
Click a group's count to see its

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:36.690
leads.

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:38.240
Age starts when the lead enters

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.290
Follow-up or Not interested.

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:41.810
Editing notes or switching between

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:43.540
those two outcomes does not restart

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.340
the clock.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.870
Review prior notes and contact

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.770
preferences before reaching out.

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.490
Finish with a clear pipeline.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.030
Deal pipeline shows the active

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.740
stages and the number of leads in

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:53.610
each one.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.120
Click a stage count to work that

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:55.840
group.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.720
Follow-up and Not interested leads

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.370
are handled in Follow-ups, and Do

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:01.590
Not Contact leads are excluded.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.580
Your daily routine is simple: review

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.630
your assigned prospects, prepare,

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.530
call, share your personal checkout

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.920
link with permission, and save the

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:09.730
outcome.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.280
Return to Team playbook whenever you

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.390
need the training or sales guidance.
